  "decision_conditions": [
    "&lt;p&gt;The host dwelling is unsuitable for conversion from Class C3 to C4 in that it will result in the loss of a family-sized unit of less than 124sqm. The principle of development is therefore unacceptable. It will be an unsustainable form of development that causes harm to the housing size and mix of the borough, which directly conflicts with Policy 15 of the adopted Waltham Forest Local Plan LP1 (2024).&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;",
    "&lt;p&gt;Two of the five bedrooms within the property fail to reach the minimum internal space standards expected for HMO accommodation. This will create substandard residential accommodation for occupiers at below the expected space standards set by the Local Plan, which is to the detriment of continued enjoyment of the dwelling and will result in a poor amenity provision for occupiers. This is contrary to the objectives of Policies 20 and 57 of the Local Plan.&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;",
    "&lt;p&gt;The proposal fails to provide adequate provision for secure, on-site cycle storage facilities and therefore fails to promote sustainable methods of transport. This is contrary to the aims of Policies 20 and 61 of the adopted Waltham Forest Local Plan LP1 (2024), which seek to promote sustainable methods of transport for future occupiers.&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;",
    "&lt;p&gt;In the absence of a legal agreement, the proposal fails to provide the necessary financial contributions to secure adequate mitigation against the Epping Forest Special Area of Conservation and therefore fails to comply with Policy 81 of the adopted Waltham Forest Local Plan LP1 (2024) and the Supplementary Planning Document - Planning Obligations (2017).&lt;/p&gt;",
    "&lt;p&gt;In the absence of a legal agreement to restrict current and future occupiers in obtaining on-street parking permits, the proposal constitutes unsustainable development in that it does not promote sustainable transport, which conflicts with the objectives of Policies 60 and 66 of the adopted Waltham Forest Local Plan LP1 (2024).&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;"
  ],
